  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1236 PM CDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nThere remains some hope for rain later this week for at least parts \nof our area as an elongated ridge axis retreats slightly. This will \nallow for weakly unsettled NNW flow to overspread much of the \npanhandles, with some of this convective potential spilling south \nacross our N-NW counties. Most of this potential looks to favor the \nevening and overnight from Wednesday through Friday, although the \nlatest deterministic and ensemble runs tend to favor Friday evening \nwhich is reflected in this latest forecast. The upper high center \nremains anchored near the Four Corners through the weekend, so this \nwill keep our highs around the century mark each day with low NBM \nprobabilities (<40%) of 105 or hotter anywhere in the forecast\narea.",
